 "derived_from": [],
 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "The equation <span data-math=\"h = 2s + 50\">h = 2s + 50</span> is used to estimate a person’s height in inches, <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>, based on women’s shoe size, <span data-math=\"s\">s</span>.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511328,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Estimate the height of a child who wears women’s shoe size 0.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"h = 2s + 50\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"h = 2\\left( 0 \\right) + 50 = 0 + 50 = 50\"></span></p>\n<p>The estimated height is 50 inches.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "50 inches"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511329,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Estimate the height of a woman with shoe size 8.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"h = 2s + 50\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"h = 2\\left( 8 \\right) + 50 = 16 + 50 = 66\"></span></p>\n<p>The estimated height is 66 inches.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "66 inches"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511330,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Interpret the slope and <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>-intercept of the equation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "For every increase in shoe size, the estimated height increases by two inches. The intercept says that for a shoe size of 0, the estimated height is 50 inches."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The slope, 2, means that the height <span data-math=\"h\">h</span> increases 2 inches when the shoe size(s) increases 1 size."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511331,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Graph the equation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Plot the point (0, 50). Use the slope <span data-math=\"\\left( {m = 2 = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{2}{1}} \\right)\"></span> to find another point. From (0, 50), count up 2 and right 1 to determine another point. Plot this point. Connect the two points with a line."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>-intercept means that when the shoe size is 0, the woman’s height is 50 inches.\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBZ3NOIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--761a82f0efc0890709eb82d82b76646e9b05e850/CS_Figure_05_08_028.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 20 to 140, in increments of 20. The line passes through the points, (negative 30, 0), (0, 50), and (40, 130). Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
